From 2dde3a523c9ad1d596520929eb41a5867c057a74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeheartgold-3ds bootstrap <bootstrap@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 05:51:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] os: count the hardware timers in software (SDK_PORT_3DS)

The DS timers count by themselves; the port counts them from a real clock
(3ds_port/nitro/src/port_timer.c), so it must bring the counters up to date
before the tick is read. The DS text is unchanged: gcc-10 -E -P of the file
without SDK_PORT_3DS (with -DSDK_ARM9) has 0 diff lines against the file before
this patch. Rebased from Platinum patch 0013 (os_tick.c half); HGSS has no
OSi_GetTick_noProfile, so only OS_GetTick and OS_GetTickLo are synced, with
plain guarded calls rather than a null macro, so the Metrowerks build
preprocesses byte-identically. The OS_SetTimerCount/Control half is the
timer_shared.h hunk of patch 1402: OS_InitTick, OS_SetTick and OSi_CountUpTick
go through those hooked inlines and need no changes here.

Tests: tests/sdk/os_timer/run.sh builds os_tick.c with the survey flags and
runs 23 checks against stub port functions: SetTimerCount/Control reach the
port with the right id and value and leave the registers untouched, OS_InitTick
issues the reserve/off/zero/on sequence, OS_GetTick returns the counter plus
the canned low word (with the pending-interrupt carry case), OS_GetTickLo
returns the low word, OS_SetTick sets the counter and re-arms, OSi_CountUpTick
bumps the counter, and both readers sync first. Against the tree without this
patch and 1402 the run fails 15 checks; dropping the OS_GetTickLo sync fails
one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/os/os_tick.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/os/os_tick.c b/src/os/os_tick.c
index 79733d2..f303ce3 100644
--- a/src/os/os_tick.c
+++ b/src/os/os_tick.c
@@ -8,8 +8,14 @@ BOOL OSi_NeedResetTimer = FALSE;
 #define OSi_TICK_TIMER         OS_TIMER_0
 #define OSi_TICK_IE_TIMER      OS_IE_TIMER0
 
-void OSi_CountUpTick(void);
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+/* 3DS port: bring the software timers up to date before reading one
+ * (3ds_port/nitro/src/port_timer.c). The call sites below are guarded, so the
+ * Metrowerks build preprocesses exactly as before. */
+void NitroPort_SyncTimers(void);
+#endif
 
+void OSi_CountUpTick(void);
 void OS_InitTick(void) {
     if (OSi_UseTick) {
         return;
@@ -46,6 +52,9 @@ OSTick OS_GetTick(void) {
     vu64 countH;
     OSIntrMode enabled = OS_DisableInterrupts();
 
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+    NitroPort_SyncTimers();
+#endif
     countL = *(REGType16 *)((u32)REG_TM0CNT_L_ADDR + OSi_TICK_TIMER * 4);
     countH = OSi_TickCounter & 0xffffffffffffULL;
     if (reg_OS_IF & OSi_TICK_IE_TIMER && !(countL & 0x8000)) {
@@ -56,6 +65,9 @@ OSTick OS_GetTick(void) {
 }
 
 u16 OS_GetTickLo(void) {
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+    NitroPort_SyncTimers();
+#endif
     return *(REGType16 *)((u32)REG_TM0CNT_L_ADDR + OSi_TICK_TIMER * 4);
 }
 
